# Add project specific R8 rules here.
# AGP combines every keep rule file in src/main/keepRules and passes them to R8.
#
# For more details, see
#   https://d.android.com/r/tools/r8/keep-rules

# WorkManager builds Workers by reflection, from the class name it persisted in
# its own database — nothing in our code ever constructs one. R8 sees that,
# keeps the class (its name is written into the work request) and strips the
# constructor, which fails only at runtime and only in a minified build:
#
#   java.lang.NoSuchMethodException:
#       com.hanifedma.waterline.notify.WatchdogWorker.<init> [...]
#
# The symptom is quiet: the app works, the timer works, and only the
# fifteen-minute watchdog that repairs a killed timer silently never runs.
-keep class * extends androidx.work.ListenableWorker {
    <init>(android.content.Context, androidx.work.WorkerParameters);
}
